   "text": "I read the structure as a bicyclic-looking but single-ring peptide: a disulfide-cyclised core carrying an N-terminal betaine-type cap and a long lipidated C-terminal tail. This is my reading of the drawing, and I could not count the long fatty-acid chain exactly.\n\n**Cyclic core (clockwise from the top right):**\n- An N-terminal Lys(\u03b5-succinyl) residue, acetylated on its \u03b1-nitrogen, sits on the right-hand penicillamine (Pen, an S\u2013S bridged CMe2 residue).\n- The ring then runs Pen \u2192 Asn \u2192 Thr \u2192 7-methyl-Trp \u2192 Lys(\u03b5-NHAc) \u2192 Pen, closed by the S\u2013S bond between the two CMe2 carbons.\n\n**N-terminal cap:** the succinyl group is amidated by a trimethylammonio-\u03b2-amino acid, Me3N\u207a\u2013CH2\u2013CH(NH\u2013)\u2013CH2\u2013COOH.\n\n**C-terminal chain from the left Pen:**\n- The left Pen's carbonyl is bonded to the NH of Tyr(O\u2013CH2CH2NH2).\n- This is followed by 2-Nal, then 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid, Glu, Asn and 3-pyridylalanine.\n- Next come N-methyl-Gly and Lys-NH2.\n- The Lys \u03b5-nitrogen carries two \u2013C(=O)CH2OCH2CH2OCH2CH2NH\u2013 units, then \u03b3-Glu, then a C18 diacid.\n\nI took the diacid as C(=O)(CH2)16COOH, the semaglutide-type chain. The drawn zigzag is long and I assumed this length rather than counting every vertex.\n\nStereocentres use the usual L-amino-acid configuration, and the stereo at the two Pen carbons and the trimethylammonium-bearing carbon is a best guess from the wedges.\n\nSMILES: C[N+](C)(C)C[C@@H](CC(=O)O)NC(=O)CCC(=O)NCCCC[C@H](NC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)O)C(=O)O)C(N)=O)C(C)(C)SSC1(C)C"
